Joost Wolf                                                26 - 5 - 1995
Dept. Theor. Prod. Ecology
Wageningen Agric. Univ.


To: John Orr, E.C.U., Univ. of Oxford


Dear John,   

In the following some information on the 82 files that I have sent to you. 
There are 46 files for Rothamsted, both baseline and scenario climate,
and 36 files for Seville, both baseline and scenario climate. Results 
are all for wheat and the data in each file are given in the way described 
in your fax of 24 May.

Explanation of the file name, e.g. ROBASMP1 or SEHIVW2 :

RO= Rothamsted, SE= Seville;
BAS= baseline, 66= transient dec. 66-75, 31= transient dec. 31-40
    HI=UKHI, LO= UKLO ;
M= data from Micha (summer 1994); E= data from Elaine (recent) , 
    for baseline and for transient dec. 66-75 scenario both are given;
D= downscaled, otherwise normal scenarios;
V= change in variability in climate data set;
P= potential (irrigated) production; W= water-limited production;
1= present atmosph. CO2; 2= increased atmosph. CO2 as given for
    each scenario.

If this is not clear, please let me know.

Kind regards,

Joost
